{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"e649ef40336508b50cf38eb24e3e5e91dad83dc1e8f44d4707f1df7a9bbfbc80","slug":"blog.2018.my-workflow","location":"/blog/2018/my-workflow.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"My weekly workflow","tags":["productivity"],"date":"2018-10-26","content_includes_title":false,"authors":[{"id":"chris","nameParsed":{"literal":"Chris Holdgraf","given":"Chris","family":"Holdgraf"},"name":"Chris Holdgraf","orcid":"0000-0002-2391-0678","affiliations":["affiliations-myst-generated-uid-0","affiliations-myst-generated-uid-1"],"url":"https://chrisholdgraf.com","github":"choldgraf","twitter":"choldgraf"}],"github":"https://github.com/choldgraf/choldgraf.github.io","affiliations":[{"name":"2i2c","url":"https://2i2c.org","id":"affiliations-myst-generated-uid-0"},{"name":"Project Jupyter","url":"https://jupyter.org","id":"affiliations-myst-generated-uid-1"}],"abbreviations":{"LF":"The Linux Foundation","JF":"The Jupyter Foundation","JEC":"Jupyter Executive Council","JFB":"The Jupyter Foundation Board","SSC":"Software Steering Council","OSPO":"Open Source Program Office"},"numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"source_url":"https://github.com/choldgraf/choldgraf.github.io/blob/main/blog/2018/my-workflow.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/choldgraf/choldgraf.github.io/edit/main/blog/2018/my-workflow.md","thumbnail":"/_public/trello-board-project-9eebd9af43c8c575561241d312bcfdeb.png","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"my-workflow.md","url":"/_public/my-workflow-64898c013fca0ca4675ca27bd5ba5e74.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":15,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I’ve had a bunch of conversations with friends who were interested in how to\nkeep track of the various projects they’re working on, and to prioritize their\ntime over the course of a week. I thought it might be helpful to post my own\napproach to planning time throughout the week in case it’s useful for others to\nriff off of.","position":{"start":{"line":11,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"key":"s9XCThnYXK"}],"key":"nycgxH1EI7"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"General principles","position":{"start":{"line":17,"column":1},"end":{"line":17,"column":1}},"key":"FOF0Ygi3kb"}],"identifier":"general-principles","label":"General principles","html_id":"general-principles","implicit":true,"key":"YhgVZcwJ6Z"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"First off, a few general principles that I use to guide my thinking on planning\nout the week.","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"hyhucq9cLw"}],"key":"S5ilLvJTeO"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":24,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Be intentional.","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"ehs2wwaDX5"}],"key":"SjiEd9I2dp"},{"type":"text","value":" This seems obvious, but I find that if I don’t explicitly define\nwhat I want to work on, I have more of those “where the heck did the day go” kinds\nof weeks.","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"icJAATzzqj"}],"key":"zDrzKCg1dY"}],"key":"gamBwgZwaF"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":27,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Be strategic.","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"wZ2cny8SF9"}],"key":"G9fYla8odH"},{"type":"text","value":" There are only so many hours in the day, which means that I need to be\ncareful about what I commit to spending time on. I try to figure out what are the most\nimportant things to do, and ensure I make space for this work before other stuff.","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"fWxXmRMmgl"}],"key":"LXXas5nW3g"}],"key":"x9CIfOuUJe"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":30,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Be (conservatively) realistic.","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"ytePtjUsDZ"}],"key":"Hx9b0ExAII"},{"type":"text","value":" I often get too optimistic with my time and energy levels.\nSometimes you’re tired, sometimes you get distracted, sometimes new work pops up you didn’t\naccount for. For this reason, I only budget about ","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"FV5rwvWUEQ"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"20 hours of diligent work a week","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"BgOie6gnxB"}],"key":"CAhofj9iQK"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":28,"column":1},"end":{"line":28,"column":1}},"key":"HeuXqPmWND"}],"key":"mzKD5bEOXv"}],"key":"GSy7D4RF1u"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":32,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Be flexible.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"rFZiuVN6Oc"}],"key":"WUn7Tagy9J"},{"type":"text","value":" Finally, don’t worry about following the plan obsessively. Use it as a guide,\nnot a set of chains. If it’s worth re-prioritizing, that’s fine!","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"KaXpXLObhI"}],"key":"cIz39KEiC9"}],"key":"i13XcVVwsO"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Be diligent.","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"rO6Ix4wRvG"}],"key":"qIEpZiGPMu"},{"type":"text","value":" That said, whenever the plans ","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"Ug1tJHDIY0"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"do","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"rvc9oQoeUI"}],"key":"cekZCLk0nG"},{"type":"text","value":" change, make sure that this is written down\nsomewhere so that I know I’m being intentional about it.","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"mKAFp5YnC4"}],"key":"Hbn74GjIN4"}],"key":"a6FDlSdjGb"}],"key":"nC7kS9kEVE"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"What tools do I use?","position":{"start":{"line":36,"column":1},"end":{"line":36,"column":1}},"key":"Wi2t929vah"}],"identifier":"what-tools-do-i-use","label":"What tools do I use?","html_id":"what-tools-do-i-use","implicit":true,"key":"aDUWbBVped"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"OK so what does this process actually look like? Here’s a general approach:","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"aGOrNMKrqK"}],"key":"akneqlrstN"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I use ","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"mGDzPGALeC"},{"type":"link","url":"https://trello.com/","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trello","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"x4oM1wE3aO"}],"key":"POboVb8Ndu"}],"urlSource":"https://trello.com/","key":"GzgPt0Tr7j"},{"type":"text","value":" for managing most of the projects that I work on each week. For those who aren’t familiar,\nTrello is a web app that lets you organize “cards” into vertical lists. It’s useful for Kanban-style\nproject management, and is super popular in technical circles.","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"nUpZ4L9ySN"}],"key":"rCOOcQyvCo"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I use two kinds of Trello boards, “project” boards, and my “weekly” board.","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"tazHhw3otU"}],"key":"wjSUY4s6Os"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Project boards","position":{"start":{"line":46,"column":1},"end":{"line":46,"column":1}},"key":"hcLFeASyIc"}],"identifier":"project-boards","label":"Project boards","html_id":"project-boards","implicit":true,"key":"I4OcDhHDwL"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Project boards are project-specific. They’re organized in four primary columns.","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"key":"we5I1ck1Kl"}],"key":"SqMzFZ5J5r"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Info","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"RJw51893bd"}],"key":"RhnQjXbLmc"},{"type":"text","value":" has cards with information about that project. For example, links, notes, attachments, etc.","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"e3Qj2I3tBT"}],"key":"hYROMo08Gc"}],"key":"zjUxyF9xji"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"ToDo","position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"key":"SZxjdm9FzJ"}],"key":"CxtZOYr9wl"},{"type":"text","value":" has cards representing tasks that I’ll do eventually. These tend to be more abstract and\nwill evolve over time.","position":{"start":{"line":51,"column":1},"end":{"line":51,"column":1}},"key":"XDUXxfUhpD"}],"key":"wMNth7Xwou"}],"key":"h4nhPBfBUN"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"XhPFsrXGvv"}],"key":"gBLmJM92G4"},{"type":"text","value":" has cards representing actionable tasks that I’ll do soon.","position":{"start":{"line":53,"column":1},"end":{"line":53,"column":1}},"key":"SgOLdJdmBr"}],"key":"smJ9QR4GKK"}],"key":"saNcLCAFn4"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":55,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Doing","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"key":"FNCVU43Rzu"}],"key":"uiFW6jwGFQ"},{"type":"text","value":" is a special list that I’ll explain later. It’s where cards go when I’m working on them currently.","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"key":"RoiP2p4nvB"}],"key":"xWnF1Zbj51"}],"key":"JnWejcPzK1"}],"key":"hZ9ZyGv2z5"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":58,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The other major component of the projcet board is a collection of “Done” lists. At the end of each\nweek, and cards that are finished get moved into a list named like so: ","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"yT1mIyfEkb"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Done - Week NN","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"KfVQ8wIKLC"}],"key":"ITkUSuw0kV"},{"type":"text","value":" where “NN” is the\nnumber of the current week.","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"EodAxSR9q9"}],"key":"sour7q8o0Q"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":61,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I keep a short-list of currently-active projects that I’m working on. These are “starred” and show up at\nthe top of the Trello board list to the left.","position":{"start":{"line":60,"column":1},"end":{"line":60,"column":1}},"key":"Hg9LMkDVKk"}],"key":"rEg2AGCNag"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here’s an example of a project board:","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"PG6h2pHE6l"}],"key":"ux1TRPGvxx"},{"type":"image","url":"/_public/trello-board-project-9eebd9af43c8c575561241d312bcfdeb.png","position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"key":"Xt0TmcvrBh","urlSource":"../../images/2018/trello-board-project.png"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Weekly board","position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"key":"RnldWADlio"}],"identifier":"weekly-board","label":"Weekly board","html_id":"weekly-board","implicit":true,"key":"TA6NBKbrxD"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":72,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The other major Trello board that I use is my “weekly” board. This is basically a to-do list for my week.\nIt’s got one list per project, and each card represents a to-do item for that project. There is one-to-one\nmapping between lists in this board and project boards that the cards come from.","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"kgdZgASGtQ"}],"key":"kOp5EclUtV"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"As I work on cards throughout the week, I move them into another list called “Done”. Once the card is there,\nit means that I’ve finished that task for the week.","position":{"start":{"line":74,"column":1},"end":{"line":74,"column":1}},"key":"ithewtIqsx"}],"key":"GES2aNqIZD"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":79,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"An additional component is that each card is assigned a number of ","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"key":"lqmL0kZTDz"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"hours needed to complete the card","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"key":"fstzCXerRG"}],"key":"r63Bh6uG00"},{"type":"text","value":".\nI try to keep the total number of hours on this board to <= 20. I’ve found that this is a realistic\nbalance between “enough hours to actually get stuff done” and “not so many hours that I won’t finish them”.","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"key":"y4Hhg0IkQA"}],"key":"maTAU9UlTl"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":82,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"To assign and keep track of the hours with each card, I use a chrome extension called ","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"RemCr4xQbW"},{"type":"link","url":"https://chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/plus-for-trello-time-trac/gjjpophepkbhejnglcmkdnncmaanojkf?hl=en","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Plus for Trello","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"G7GRw7N6a5"}],"key":"DGeMRRpOCt"}],"urlSource":"https://chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/plus-for-trello-time-trac/gjjpophepkbhejnglcmkdnncmaanojkf?hl=en","key":"OobvSXCyFx"},{"type":"text","value":". This\nadds fields for “estimated” and “spent” hours that I update over the week.","position":{"start":{"line":81,"column":1},"end":{"line":81,"column":1}},"key":"w1uxGMv5dP"}],"key":"CwGnWpvXFw"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1},"end":{"line":84,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here’s an example of a weekly board:","position":{"start":{"line":84,"column":1},"end":{"line":84,"column":1}},"key":"l8cZZ3FaUT"}],"key":"nfN8WGa9XJ"},{"type":"image","url":"/_public/trello-board-active-84a36e29270148960d5ec2e8cb55641b.png","position":{"start":{"line":86,"column":1},"end":{"line":86,"column":1}},"key":"jxNqmjhteo","urlSource":"../../images/2018/trello-board-active.png"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":89,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"How does this work in practice?","position":{"start":{"line":89,"column":1},"end":{"line":89,"column":1}},"key":"sxZqg4SBUm"}],"identifier":"how-does-this-work-in-practice","label":"How does this work in practice?","html_id":"how-does-this-work-in-practice","implicit":true,"key":"FQjwAS9qG3"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I use a tool called ","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"rFLk3j7Fwh"},{"type":"link","url":"https://butlerfortrello.com/","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Butler for Trello","position":{"start":{"line":91,"column":1},"end":{"line":91,"column":1}},"key":"xEhyyVAP5i"}],"key":"zndUaQ6vBi"}],"urlSource":"https://butlerfortrello.com/","key":"zn1B41xGli"},{"type":"text","value":" (BFT) to manage how cards flow through this system.\nLets you automate various tasks in Trello by writing messages that it parses 